            <title>[LU-20812] mdc: mdc_create() leaks the request on a bad mkdir reply</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20812</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In mdc_create(), after a successful reint for a directory, two error exits return before *request = req:&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;br/&gt;
  - req_capsule_server_get(&amp;amp;RMF_MDT_BODY) returns NULL → RETURN(-EPROTO)&lt;br/&gt;
  - req_capsule_server_sized_get(&amp;amp;RMF_MDT_MD) returns NULL → RETURN(-EPROTO)&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;br/&gt;
The caller never gets the request, so it is never put. The request leaks, and with it the import reference taken by ptlrpc_request_alloc(). A short or malformed mkdir reply from the MDT can trigger either one.&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;br/&gt;
Fix: ptlrpc_req_put(req) before both returns, or set *request = req first so the caller drops it.&lt;br/&gt;
  &lt;br/&gt;
Found during review of &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/65026" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/65026&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20050" title="ptlrpc: fix sepol error handling in ptlrpc_connect_import_locked" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20050"&gt;LU-20050&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
